From bc61d9072ca51c3a4a6e0d435d4642c8f60a486c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:47:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): run the over-plane composite on every exit, not
 just a woven one

With the switch above injected, device logs showed the split working perfectly
("plane-split: tiles=1 quads=72 over_set=5 ... difference_clip=1") while
"inline-3D occlusion composite:" never appeared: the page raster was
difference-clipped -- the 2D removed -- and the over-plane was painted, and then
never composited back. Punch without repair, which is exactly the reported
symptom.

The plane split is two halves that must always travel together. The compositor
thread PUNCHES unconditionally once --inline-3d-occlusion is on. The GPU thread
REPAIRS. But the repair sat at the very bottom of phase (B), behind five exits
that are all WEAVE preconditions and none of which has anything to do with the
over-plane -- a plain window-sized RGBA8 SharedImage the renderer painted:

  1. the browser#87 liveness gate (batch && !wove_this_frame),
  2. displayxr_shared_woven_mailbox_.IsZero()  ("nothing woven yet"),
  3. ProduceSkia(woven) failure,
  4. BeginScopedReadAccess(woven) failure,
  5. CreateSkImage(woven) failure.

The asymmetry is structural: the punch happens on the compositor thread from
the switch alone, while the repair carried four extra GPU-thread preconditions
on top of the liveness gate. Any frame that failed to weave silently kept the
punch and dropped the repair, and what the user sees is the bare woven tile
where their overlay should be.

Hoist the body into composite_over_plane_android() and call it on all five
exits plus the healthy path. Unchanged on the healthy path, byte for byte:
whole-window kSrcOver, AFTER the woven draw-back, outside the frosted clip
scope, skipped when the DP already staged the plane as its overlay atlas
(browser#18 v4) or when R7's window-size check fails. It must stay unclipped by
the woven rects -- clipping it is the inverse bug, browser#120's "2D visible,
tile dark".

The flush moves INSIDE the lambda. |over_access| is scoped there, and the 0064
lesson is that an access released before the SUBMIT draws nothing; on the four
early-exit paths that flush is the only one there is. A per-call latch keeps a
double composite unreachable.

The marker is LOG(WARNING), not VLOG(1) as on Windows, and reports why it
skipped: a default logcat is what a device capture collects, so the Windows
arm's VLOG is invisible there -- which is why the absence of the line in the
capture that opened this bug could not be read as evidence either way. Throttled
first-3-then-1-in-120; never per frame.

Preserved: the belt's rect-scoped woven draw-back and its SurfaceControl gate,
patch 0081's UNRESOLVED withhold semantics, the frosted difference clip, and the
fix14 commits. The three DEVICE-REJECTED fix15 commits (813ca01, 7872348,
4163f1b) are reverted immediately before this one.
---
 .../skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc        | 209 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 163 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc b/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
index 57de8a330f788..95041858acc84 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display_embedder/skia_output_surface_impl_on_gpu.cc
@@ -4862,6 +4862,135 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::WeaveCompositedSurface(SkSurface* output,
   std::vector<gfx::Rect> frosted_rects = std::move(inline_3d_frosted_rects_);
   inline_3d_frosted_rects_.clear();
 #endif
+
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+  // ---- Phase-2 over-plane composite, hoisted so EVERY exit runs it ---------
+  //
+  // WHY THIS IS A LAMBDA AND NOT THE INLINE BLOCK IT USED TO BE.
+  //
+  // The plane split is two halves that must always travel together: the
+  // compositor thread PUNCHES the lifted 2D out of the page raster with a
+  // kDifference clip (DirectRenderer::ComputeInline3dPlaneSplit + SkiaRenderer),
+  // and this side REPAIRS it by compositing the over-plane back on top. The
+  // punch is unconditional once --inline-3d-occlusion is on. The repair sat at
+  // the very bottom of phase (B), behind five separate exits:
+  //
+  //   1. the browser#87 liveness gate (batch && !wove_this_frame),
+  //   2. displayxr_shared_woven_mailbox_.IsZero()  ("nothing woven yet"),
+  //   3. ProduceSkia(woven) failure,
+  //   4. BeginScopedReadAccess(woven) failure,
+  //   5. CreateSkImage(woven) failure.
+  //
+  // Every one of those is a WEAVE precondition. None of them has anything to do
+  // with the over-plane, which is a plain window-sized RGBA8 SharedImage the
+  // RENDERER painted. So any frame that failed to weave silently dropped the
+  // repair while keeping the punch: the 2D content was removed from the page
+  // and never put back, and what the user sees is the bare woven tile where
+  // their overlay should be. That is the reported defect, and it is why the
+  // composite is now a callable that runs on all five paths.
+  //
+  // Whole-window, kSrcOver, LAST — unchanged from what it replaces. Outside the
+  // tile rects the plane is transparent by construction (the paint clips every
+  // draw into a tile rect), so a whole-window sample cannot touch 2D chrome
+  // elsewhere; and it must NOT be clipped to the woven rects, which is the
+  // inverse bug (browser#120: "2D visible, tile dark" when the draw-back is
+  // clipped so as to exclude the plane's region).
+  //
+  // Latched per call site: the gate paths return, so a double composite is not
+  // reachable today, but a latch is cheaper than relying on that.
+  auto flush_output_android = [&]() {
+    std::vector<GrBackendSemaphore> empty_sem;
+    FlushSurface(output, empty_sem, /*scoped_write_access=*/nullptr);
+    if (gr_context()) {
+      gr_context()->submit();
+    }
+    if (graphite_shared_context()) {
+      graphite_shared_context()->submit();
+    }
+  };
+  bool over_plane_composited_android = false;
+  auto composite_over_plane_android = [&]() -> bool {
+    if (over_plane_composited_android) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    // (browser#18 v4) dp_overlay_staged_android: the runtime's DP already
+    // composited this plane INTO the woven output for this frame, so drawing it
+    // again here would double-composite every translucent scrim.
+    //
+    // Risk guard R7: a plane that is not exactly window-sized would smear if
+    // sampled 1:1, so skip rather than stretch. Transient (one frame after a
+    // resize, until the renderer paints a new plane).
+    const bool size_ok = inline_3d_over_plane_size_ == window_bounds.size();
+    const bool eligible = inline3d_occlusion_enabled_ &&
+                          !dp_overlay_staged_android &&
+                          !inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_.IsZero() && size_ok;
+    bool drawn = false;
+    if (eligible) {
+      auto over_rep = shared_image_representation_factory_->ProduceSkia(
+          inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_, context_state_.get());
+      std::vector<GrBackendSemaphore> obegin_sem, oend_sem;
+      auto over_access =
+          over_rep ? over_rep->BeginScopedReadAccess(&obegin_sem, &oend_sem)
+                   : nullptr;
+      if (over_access) {
+        sk_sp<SkImage> over_img =
+            over_access->CreateSkImage(context_state_.get());
+        if (over_img) {
+          if (!obegin_sem.empty()) {
+            output->wait(obegin_sem.size(), obegin_sem.data(),
+                         /*deleteSemaphoresAfterWait=*/false);
+          }
+          const SkRect win = SkRect::MakeXYWH(
+              window_bounds.x(), window_bounds.y(), window_bounds.width(),
+              window_bounds.height());
+          SkPaint over_paint;
+          over_paint.setBlendMode(SkBlendMode::kSrcOver);
+          // NEAREST + kStrict: a device-pixel-exact 1:1 blit of pixels the
+          // renderer already rasterised at device scale. Any filtering here
+          // would resample the page's own text.
+          out_canvas->drawImageRect(
+              over_img.get(), win, win,
+              SkSamplingOptions(SkFilterMode::kNearest), &over_paint,
+              SkCanvas::kStrict_SrcRectConstraint);
+          drawn = true;
+          over_plane_composited_android = true;
+        }
+      }
+      // The 0064 lesson: |over_access| must outlive the SUBMIT, not just the
+      // draw call, or Ganesh reads a released texture at flush time and the
+      // draw shows nothing. |over_access| is scoped to this lambda, so the
+      // flush belongs HERE — not at the call site. On the healthy path the
+      // woven access is still alive too (this runs inside its scope), so the
+      // draw-back is flushed by the same call and its own trailing flush is a
+      // no-op; on the four early-exit paths this is the only flush there is.
+      if (drawn) {
+        flush_output_android();
+      }
+    }
+    // Self-verifying marker for the next device capture. LOG(WARNING), not
+    // VLOG(1): the Windows arm's VLOG is invisible in a default logcat, which
+    // is exactly why "inline-3D occlusion composite:" never appeared in the
+    // capture that opened this bug and the absence could not be read as
+    // evidence either way. Throttled first-3-then-1-in-120, never per frame.
+    if (inline3d_occlusion_enabled_) {
+      static int over_dbg = 0;
+      const int n = over_dbg++;
+      if (n < 3 || (n % 120) == 0) {
+        LOG(WARNING) << "[DisplayXR] inline-3D occlusion composite: over-plane "
+                     << inline_3d_over_plane_size_.ToString()
+                     << " drawn=" << drawn << " skipped=" << !drawn
+                     << " (mailbox="
+                     << (inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_.IsZero() ? "zero" : "ok")
+                     << " size_ok=" << size_ok
+                     << " dp_overlay=" << dp_overlay_staged_android
+                     << " window=" << window_bounds.size().ToString()
+                     << " events=" << (n + 1) << ")";
+      }
+    }
+    return drawn;
+  };
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+
   // (browser#87) Liveness gate: skip the Phase (B) draw-back entirely when this
   // frame wove nothing, rather than blitting a woven texture that still holds
   // the previous page's pixels. Batch mode only: the batch weave completes
@@ -4881,6 +5010,14 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::WeaveCompositedSurface(SkSurface* output,
     // gate: async mode keeps the last woven output visible by contract, so it
     // has no hole to fill.
     recovery_draw(/*only_unsubmitted=*/false);
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+    // The punch already happened this frame; the weave did not. Repair anyway,
+    // ON TOP of the mono recovery draw above (over means over), or the lifted
+    // 2D is simply gone. recovery_draw() brings its own flush and this draw
+    // lands after it; the composite flushes itself, so nothing is left
+    // unsubmitted on this path.
+    composite_over_plane_android();
+#endif
     return;
   }
 
@@ -5471,7 +5608,11 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::WeaveCompositedSurface(SkSurface* output,
   }
 
   if (displayxr_shared_woven_mailbox_.IsZero()) {
-    return;  // nothing woven yet — leave the raw SBS content
+    // Nothing woven yet — leave the raw SBS content. But the plane split's
+    // punch is not conditional on the weave, so the over-plane repair still
+    // has to run or the lifted 2D is lost on every pre-weave frame.
+    composite_over_plane_android();
+    return;
   }
 
   bool drew_any = false;
@@ -5480,17 +5621,26 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::WeaveCompositedSurface(SkSurface* output,
     auto woven_rep = shared_image_representation_factory_->ProduceSkia(
         displayxr_shared_woven_mailbox_, context_state_.get());
     if (!woven_rep) {
+      // Weave precondition failed; the over-plane is not a weave resource and
+      // its punch already landed, so composite it before giving up.
+      composite_over_plane_android();
       return;
     }
     std::vector<GrBackendSemaphore> wbegin_sem, wend_sem;
     auto woven_access = woven_rep->BeginScopedReadAccess(&wbegin_sem,
                                                          &wend_sem);
     if (!woven_access) {
+      // Weave precondition failed; the over-plane is not a weave resource and
+      // its punch already landed, so composite it before giving up.
+      composite_over_plane_android();
       return;
     }
     sk_sp<SkImage> woven_img =
         woven_access->CreateSkImage(context_state_.get());
     if (!woven_img) {
+      // Weave precondition failed; the over-plane is not a weave resource and
+      // its punch already landed, so composite it before giving up.
+      composite_over_plane_android();
       return;
     }
     if (!wbegin_sem.empty()) {
@@ -5749,52 +5899,19 @@ void SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu::WeaveCompositedSurface(SkSurface* output,
     // per-pixel contract and the R9 no-double-count rule). LAST, so it wins
     // over the draw-back — over means over.
     //
-    // (browser#18 v4) ...unless the runtime's DP already composited that plane
-    // for us this frame. It composites INTO the woven output, so the pixels
-    // arrive through the per-rect blit above and drawing the plane again here
-    // would double-composite every translucent scrim.
+    // The body moved into |composite_over_plane_android| above so the four
+    // early returns between here and the top of phase (B) can run it too; the
+    // behaviour on THIS, the healthy path, is byte-for-byte what it was:
+    // whole-window kSrcOver, after the woven draw-back, skipped when the DP
+    // already staged the plane as its overlay atlas.
     //
-    // The known asymmetry, stated rather than discovered later: the browser-side
-    // draw is WHOLE-WINDOW while the blit above covers only |drawn_rect| per
-    // target. Those coincide on a healthy frame (the plane is transparent
-    // outside the tile rects by construction), and diverge on a frame where a
-    // target declined its weave - there the DP path loses that tile's 2D
-    // over-content, where the browser-side path would have kept it. That is
-    // precisely why --inline-3d-dp-overlay is opt-in.
-    bool over_plane_drawn = false;
-    const bool over_plane_size_ok =
-        inline3d_occlusion_enabled_ && !dp_overlay_staged_android &&
-        !inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_.IsZero() &&
-        inline_3d_over_plane_size_ == window_bounds.size();
-    auto over_rep = over_plane_size_ok
-                        ? shared_image_representation_factory_->ProduceSkia(
-                              inline_3d_over_plane_mailbox_,
-                              context_state_.get())
-                        : nullptr;
-    std::vector<GrBackendSemaphore> obegin_sem, oend_sem;
-    auto over_access =
-        over_rep ? over_rep->BeginScopedReadAccess(&obegin_sem, &oend_sem)
-                 : nullptr;
-    if (over_access) {
-      sk_sp<SkImage> over_img =
-          over_access->CreateSkImage(context_state_.get());
-      if (over_img) {
-        if (!obegin_sem.empty()) {
-          output->wait(obegin_sem.size(), obegin_sem.data(),
-                       /*deleteSemaphoresAfterWait=*/false);
-        }
-        const SkRect win = SkRect::MakeXYWH(
-            window_bounds.x(), window_bounds.y(), window_bounds.width(),
-            window_bounds.height());
-        SkPaint over_paint;
-        over_paint.setBlendMode(SkBlendMode::kSrcOver);
-        out_canvas->drawImageRect(over_img.get(), win, win,
-                                  SkSamplingOptions(SkFilterMode::kNearest),
-                                  &over_paint,
-                                  SkCanvas::kStrict_SrcRectConstraint);
-        over_plane_drawn = true;
-      }
-    }
+    // The known asymmetry, restated: this draw is WHOLE-WINDOW while the blit
+    // above covers only |drawn_rect| per target. Those coincide on a healthy
+    // frame (the plane is transparent outside the tile rects by construction),
+    // and diverge on a frame where a target declined its weave — there the DP
+    // path loses that tile's 2D over-content, where the browser-side path keeps
+    // it. That is precisely why --inline-3d-dp-overlay is opt-in.
+    const bool over_plane_drawn = composite_over_plane_android();
 
     // ONE flush for the whole draw-back, before the read accesses release
     // (the 0064 lesson: an access released before the submit draws nothing).
